{"chunk_id": "company_history_eta::c000", "document_id": "company_history_eta", "sequence": 0, "source_start": 0, "source_end": 24, "offset_resolution": "resolved", "heading_prefix_dropped": false, "text": "Founding and Early Years", "chunker_version": "chunk-v1-legacy-chars-1000-200", "chunk_char_len": 24, "source_document_hash": "c8425307f982eadce5340c4a666ad794e6afa0a64576f09d77b9d74ca9466f97", "structure": {"section_ids": ["company_history_eta#s0"], "paragraph_ids": [], "table_ids": [], "row_ids": [], "cell_ids": [], "list_ids": [], "list_item_ids": []}}
{"chunk_id": "company_history_eta::c001", "document_id": "company_history_eta", "sequence": 1, "source_start": 0, "source_end": 364, "offset_resolution": "resolved", "heading_prefix_dropped": false, "text": "Founding and Early Years\n\nApex Computing was founded on June 8, 1998, by Dr. Margaret Liu and James Whitfield in a converted warehouse in Portland, Oregon. The initial team of 5 engineers developed ApexOS, a lightweight operating system for embedded devices. The company received its first round of funding of $2.5 million from Northwest Ventures in November 1998.", "chunker_version": "chunk-v1-legacy-chars-1000-200", "chunk_char_len": 364, "source_document_hash": "c8425307f982eadce5340c4a666ad794e6afa0a64576f09d77b9d74ca9466f97", "structure": {"section_ids": ["company_history_eta#s0"], "paragraph_ids": ["company_history_eta#s0#p1"], "table_ids": [], "row_ids": [], "cell_ids": [], "list_ids": [], "list_item_ids": []}}
{"chunk_id": "company_history_eta::c002", "document_id": "company_history_eta", "sequence": 2, "source_start": 366, "source_end": 620, "offset_resolution": "resolved", "heading_prefix_dropped": true, "text": "Founding and Early Years\n\nBy 2001, Apex Computing had grown to 45 employees and secured contracts with three major telecommunications companies. Revenue reached $8.3 million in fiscal year 2001. The company moved to its current headquarters at 500 Technology Center in March 2002.", "chunker_version": "chunk-v1-legacy-chars-1000-200", "chunk_char_len": 280, "source_document_hash": "c8425307f982eadce5340c4a666ad794e6afa0a64576f09d77b9d74ca9466f97", "structure": {"section_ids": ["company_history_eta#s0"], "paragraph_ids": ["company_history_eta#s0#p2"], "table_ids": [], "row_ids": [], "cell_ids": [], "list_ids": [], "list_item_ids": []}}
{"chunk_id": "company_history_eta::c003", "document_id": "company_history_eta", "sequence": 3, "source_start": 622, "source_end": 646, "offset_resolution": "resolved", "heading_prefix_dropped": false, "text": "Growth Phase (2003-2010)", "chunker_version": "chunk-v1-legacy-chars-1000-200", "chunk_char_len": 24, "source_document_hash": "c8425307f982eadce5340c4a666ad794e6afa0a64576f09d77b9d74ca9466f97", "structure": {"section_ids": ["company_history_eta#s1"], "paragraph_ids": [], "table_ids": [], "row_ids": [], "cell_ids": [], "list_ids": [], "list_item_ids": []}}
{"chunk_id": "company_history_eta::c004", "document_id": "company_history_eta", "sequence": 4, "source_start": 622, "source_end": 1032, "offset_resolution": "resolved", "heading_prefix_dropped": false, "text": "Growth Phase (2003-2010)\n\nThe period from 2003 to 2010 marked rapid expansion for Apex Computing. The company launched its flagship product, Apex Enterprise Suite, in September 2003 at a price point of $49,000 per license. By 2005, the company had 200 employees and annual revenue of $42 million. The company went public on NASDAQ on October 14, 2006, at an initial share price of $18.50, raising $185 million.", "chunker_version": "chunk-v1-legacy-chars-1000-200", "chunk_char_len": 410, "source_document_hash": "c8425307f982eadce5340c4a666ad794e6afa0a64576f09d77b9d74ca9466f97", "structure": {"section_ids": ["company_history_eta#s1"], "paragraph_ids": ["company_history_eta#s1#p1"], "table_ids": [], "row_ids": [], "cell_ids": [], "list_ids": [], "list_item_ids": []}}
{"chunk_id": "company_history_eta::c005", "document_id": "company_history_eta", "sequence": 5, "source_start": 1034, "source_end": 1258, "offset_resolution": "resolved", "heading_prefix_dropped": true, "text": "Growth Phase (2003-2010)\n\nInternational expansion began in 2007 with the opening of the London office. By 2010, Apex had offices in 8 countries and employed 650 people worldwide. Annual revenue reached $178 million with a net income of $23.4 million.", "chunker_version": "chunk-v1-legacy-chars-1000-200", "chunk_char_len": 250, "source_document_hash": "c8425307f982eadce5340c4a666ad794e6afa0a64576f09d77b9d74ca9466f97", "structure": {"section_ids": ["company_history_eta#s1"], "paragraph_ids": ["company_history_eta#s1#p2"], "table_ids": [], "row_ids": [], "cell_ids": [], "list_ids": [], "list_item_ids": []}}
{"chunk_id": "company_history_eta::c006", "document_id": "company_history_eta", "sequence": 6, "source_start": 1260, "source_end": 1527, "offset_resolution": "resolved", "heading_prefix_dropped": true, "text": "Growth Phase (2003-2010)\n\nYear | Revenue (USD) | Employees | Key Milestone\n2001 | $8.3M | 45 | First telecom contracts\n2003 | $18.7M | 85 | Apex Enterprise Suite launch\n2006 | $52.1M | 280 | IPO on NASDAQ\n2008 | $112.4M | 420 | London office opened\n2010 | $178.0M | 650 | Revenue exceeds $150M", "chunker_version": "chunk-v1-legacy-chars-1000-200", "chunk_char_len": 293, "source_document_hash": "c8425307f982eadce5340c4a666ad794e6afa0a64576f09d77b9d74ca9466f97", "structure": {"section_ids": ["company_history_eta#s1"], "paragraph_ids": [], "table_ids": ["company_history_eta#s1#t0"], "row_ids": ["company_history_eta#s1#t0@-1", "company_history_eta#s1#t0@0", "company_history_eta#s1#t0@1", "company_history_eta#s1#t0@2", "company_history_eta#s1#t0@3", "company_history_eta#s1#t0@4"], "cell_ids": ["company_history_eta#s1#t0@-1:0", "company_history_eta#s1#t0@-1:1", "company_history_eta#s1#t0@-1:2", "company_history_eta#s1#t0@-1:3", "company_history_eta#s1#t0@0:0", "company_history_eta#s1#t0@0:1", "company_history_eta#s1#t0@0:2", "company_history_eta#s1#t0@0:3", "company_history_eta#s1#t0@1:0", "company_history_eta#s1#t0@1:1", "company_history_eta#s1#t0@1:2", "company_history_eta#s1#t0@1:3", "company_history_eta#s1#t0@2:0", "company_history_eta#s1#t0@2:1", "company_history_eta#s1#t0@2:2", "company_history_eta#s1#t0@2:3", "company_history_eta#s1#t0@3:0", "company_history_eta#s1#t0@3:1", "company_history_eta#s1#t0@3:2", "company_history_eta#s1#t0@3:3", "company_history_eta#s1#t0@4:0", "company_history_eta#s1#t0@4:1", "company_history_eta#s1#t0@4:2", "company_history_eta#s1#t0@4:3"], "list_ids": [], "list_item_ids": []}}
{"chunk_id": "company_history_eta::c007", "document_id": "company_history_eta", "sequence": 7, "source_start": 1529, "source_end": 1559, "offset_resolution": "resolved", "heading_prefix_dropped": false, "text": "Transformation Era (2011-2020)", "chunker_version": "chunk-v1-legacy-chars-1000-200", "chunk_char_len": 30, "source_document_hash": "c8425307f982eadce5340c4a666ad794e6afa0a64576f09d77b9d74ca9466f97", "structure": {"section_ids": ["company_history_eta#s2"], "paragraph_ids": [], "table_ids": [], "row_ids": [], "cell_ids": [], "list_ids": [], "list_item_ids": []}}
{"chunk_id": "company_history_eta::c008", "document_id": "company_history_eta", "sequence": 8, "source_start": 1529, "source_end": 1896, "offset_resolution": "resolved", "heading_prefix_dropped": false, "text": "Transformation Era (2011-2020)\n\nIn 2012, Apex Computing acquired DataStream Analytics for $340 million, adding real-time data processing capabilities to its product portfolio. The acquisition added 120 engineers and brought the total employee count to 950. The combined platform, Apex DataStream, was launched in Q2 2013 at a combined license fee of $89,000 per year.", "chunker_version": "chunk-v1-legacy-chars-1000-200", "chunk_char_len": 367, "source_document_hash": "c8425307f982eadce5340c4a666ad794e6afa0a64576f09d77b9d74ca9466f97", "structure": {"section_ids": ["company_history_eta#s2"], "paragraph_ids": ["company_history_eta#s2#p1"], "table_ids": [], "row_ids": [], "cell_ids": [], "list_ids": [], "list_item_ids": []}}
{"chunk_id": "company_history_eta::c009", "document_id": "company_history_eta", "sequence": 9, "source_start": 1898, "source_end": 2217, "offset_resolution": "resolved", "heading_prefix_dropped": true, "text": "Transformation Era (2011-2020)\n\nThe cloud transition began in 2015 with the launch of Apex Cloud, a SaaS version of the enterprise suite priced at $4,900 per month. By 2018, cloud revenue represented 40 percent of total revenue. The company reached the milestone of 1,000 employees in March 2017 and annual revenue of $425 million by fiscal year 2020.", "chunker_version": "chunk-v1-legacy-chars-1000-200", "chunk_char_len": 351, "source_document_hash": "c8425307f982eadce5340c4a666ad794e6afa0a64576f09d77b9d74ca9466f97", "structure": {"section_ids": ["company_history_eta#s2"], "paragraph_ids": ["company_history_eta#s2#p2"], "table_ids": [], "row_ids": [], "cell_ids": [], "list_ids": [], "list_item_ids": []}}
{"chunk_id": "company_history_eta::c010", "document_id": "company_history_eta", "sequence": 10, "source_start": 2219, "source_end": 2245, "offset_resolution": "resolved", "heading_prefix_dropped": false, "text": "Present Day (2021-Present)", "chunker_version": "chunk-v1-legacy-chars-1000-200", "chunk_char_len": 26, "source_document_hash": "c8425307f982eadce5340c4a666ad794e6afa0a64576f09d77b9d74ca9466f97", "structure": {"section_ids": ["company_history_eta#s3"], "paragraph_ids": [], "table_ids": [], "row_ids": [], "cell_ids": [], "list_ids": [], "list_item_ids": []}}
{"chunk_id": "company_history_eta::c011", "document_id": "company_history_eta", "sequence": 11, "source_start": 2219, "source_end": 2673, "offset_resolution": "resolved", "heading_prefix_dropped": false, "text": "Present Day (2021-Present)\n\nAs of September 2025, Apex Computing employs 2,847 people across 14 offices worldwide. The company reported annual revenue of $1.24 billion for fiscal year 2024, with cloud revenue now representing 72 percent of the total. The current CEO, Dr. Sarah Chen (appointed January 2022), has overseen the integration of artificial intelligence capabilities across the product line, with the launch of Apex AI Assistant in March 2024.", "chunker_version": "chunk-v1-legacy-chars-1000-200", "chunk_char_len": 454, "source_document_hash": "c8425307f982eadce5340c4a666ad794e6afa0a64576f09d77b9d74ca9466f97", "structure": {"section_ids": ["company_history_eta#s3"], "paragraph_ids": ["company_history_eta#s3#p1"], "table_ids": [], "row_ids": [], "cell_ids": [], "list_ids": [], "list_item_ids": []}}
{"chunk_id": "company_history_eta::c012", "document_id": "company_history_eta", "sequence": 12, "source_start": 2675, "source_end": 2924, "offset_resolution": "resolved", "heading_prefix_dropped": true, "text": "Present Day (2021-Present)\n\nThe company's stock (ticker: APX) trades at approximately $142.50 per share as of September 15, 2025, giving it a market capitalization of approximately $18.7 billion. The board of directors consists of 9 members, with Dr. Liu serving as Chairwoman.", "chunker_version": "chunk-v1-legacy-chars-1000-200", "chunk_char_len": 277, "source_document_hash": "c8425307f982eadce5340c4a666ad794e6afa0a64576f09d77b9d74ca9466f97", "structure": {"section_ids": ["company_history_eta#s3"], "paragraph_ids": ["company_history_eta#s3#p2"], "table_ids": [], "row_ids": [], "cell_ids": [], "list_ids": [], "list_item_ids": []}}
{"chunk_id": "company_history_eta::c013", "document_id": "company_history_eta", "sequence": 13, "source_start": 2926, "source_end": 3148, "offset_resolution": "resolved", "heading_prefix_dropped": true, "text": "Present Day (2021-Present)\n\nCurrent Leadership\nCEO: Dr. Sarah Chen (since January 2022)\nCTO: James Whitfield (co-founder, since 1998)\nCFO: Robert Tanaka (since March 2019)\nCOO: Elena Vasquez (since June 2021)\nChairwoman: Dr. Margaret Liu (co-founder)", "chunker_version": "chunk-v1-legacy-chars-1000-200", "chunk_char_len": 250, "source_document_hash": "c8425307f982eadce5340c4a666ad794e6afa0a64576f09d77b9d74ca9466f97", "structure": {"section_ids": ["company_history_eta#s3"], "paragraph_ids": [], "table_ids": [], "row_ids": [], "cell_ids": [], "list_ids": ["company_history_eta#s3#l0"], "list_item_ids": ["company_history_eta#s3#l0#0", "company_history_eta#s3#l0#1", "company_history_eta#s3#l0#2", "company_history_eta#s3#l0#3", "company_history_eta#s3#l0#4"]}}
